Git Rebase Task Documentation
Task Overview
The Nautilus application development team requested to update an in-progress feature branch with changes from the master branch in /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/apps on the Storage Server (ststor01). The key requirements were:

Integrate master branch updates into the feature branch without losing any feature work.

Avoid generating a merge commit (accomplished via git rebase).

Push the rebased feature branch back to the remote repository (/opt/apps.git).

Infrastructure & Environment Details
Jump Host: jump-host (thor)

Storage Server: ststor01 (natasha)

Repository Path: /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/apps

Remote Repository: /opt/apps.git

Step-by-Step Execution Log
1. SSH into Storage Server
From the jump host, access ststor01:

Bash
ssh natasha@ststor01
2. Navigate to Repository Directory
Bash
cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/apps
3. Add Safe Directory Exception
Because the directory is owned by root, Git flags a dubious ownership warning. Add the exception globally/system-wide:

Bash
sudo git config --system --add safe.directory /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/apps
4. Fetch and Sync the Master Branch
Switch to the master branch and pull the latest changes from the origin remote:

Bash
sudo git checkout master
sudo git pull origin master
5. Rebase Feature Branch onto Master
Switch to the feature branch and rebase it onto master so that feature commits sit linearly on top of the latest master commits:

Bash
sudo git checkout feature
sudo git rebase master
6. Verify Git Log History
Confirm that the branch history is linear without any merge commits:

Bash
git log --oneline -n 5
Expected Output:

Plaintext
0987dfa (HEAD -> feature) Add new feature
c24cb66 (origin/master, master) Update info.txt
d82bd00 initial commit
7. Force Push Rebased Branch
Push the updated linear history of feature to the remote repository (/opt/apps.git):

Bash
sudo git push origin feature --force
Conclusion
The feature branch was successfully rebased on top of master without merge commits or data loss, and the updated branch history was pushed back to the central repository.
